      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To dismantle the \"labor disincentive\" claim, your student should introduce evidence from pilot programs showing that most recipients use the stability to pursue education, start small businesses, or care for family. They can counter by arguing that the current system often traps people in low-wage jobs out of necessity, whereas UBI provides the dignity and security needed for meaningful work. Furthermore, they can assert that human motivation is complex; UBI doesn't remove the desire to improve one's life, only the fear of utter destitution.",
